The full fresh two-claim proof closes with `#Top`. I also proved the loop claim alone, then proved the unchanged entry claim against that already-closed loop lemma; filtering the loop lemma out entirely causes symbolic unrolling to diverge, so that run is diagnostic rather than a defect. I’m now checking AST identity at K’s macro-expanded parse level and auditing the exact execution path through calls, frames, iteration, membership, and return.
